<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chōsokabe Morichika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1575–1615</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Chosokabe Morichika</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chōsokabe Morichika (1575–1615) was the last Chōsokabe lord of Tosa, a son of Motochika. He joined the western army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> in 1600, and after its defeat lost his domain, which passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamauchi-kazutoyo">Yamauchi Kazutoyo</a>. Living as a teacher in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, he joined the defenders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka-castle">Osaka Castle</a> in 1614–15; after its fall he was captured and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chosokabe-morichika.jpg" alt="Chōsokabe Morichika" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suzuki Shōnen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ch%C5%8Dsokabe_Morichika.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
